## What changed and why

**The first draft called `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(line.Product2Id)` inside a `for` loop over every line.** That method contains a SOQL query, so a 200-line quote fired 200 queries and blew through the 100-query governor limit (`System.LimitException: Too many SOQL queries: 101`).

**The fix:** pull the `Product2` records out of the loop with a single `SELECT … WHERE Id IN :productIds` query, then call **`PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily(family)`** per line. That method is pure if/else logic with no SOQL, so calling it once per row is free. The pricing rules still live exclusively in `PricingRules`; nothing was copied into the handler. The 200-line (and any larger) CPQ quote now uses exactly **one** SOQL query regardless of record count.

